From: SM-A105F Linux 6.18.54 board port
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: add SM-A105F board compatible

Give the A10 board a valid, model-specific compatible and register it in
the existing Exynos7885 board schema. Preserve the marketing description
in model, and keep the SoC compatible as the fallback. The downstream
`samsung,A10 SWA OPEN 00` string contains spaces and is not a valid compatible.

Validated against Linux v6.18.54 commit 1b357ecb321392158d507b04672ffee57bfa071d:
Samsung board-schema dt_binding_check, A10 CHECK_DTBS build, and focused
and full direct dt-validate. The compatible diagnostic is cleared. The
remaining full-validator finding is the inherited osc-clock missing
clock-frequency; no value is inferred here.

---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/samsung/samsung-boards.yaml | 1 +
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7885-a10.dts                    | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/samsung/samsung-boards.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/samsung/samsung-boards.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/samsung/samsung-boards.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/samsung/samsung-boards.yaml
@@ -223,5 +223,6 @@
       - description: Exynos7885 based boards
         items:
           - enum:
               - samsung,jackpotlte              # Samsung Galaxy A8 (2018)
+              - samsung,sm-a105f                # Samsung Galaxy A10 (SM-A105F)
           - const: samsung,exynos7885

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7885-a10.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7885-a10.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7885-a10.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7885-a10.dts
@@ -8,3 +8,3 @@
 / {
 	model = "Samsung Galaxy A10 (SM-A105F)";
-	compatible = "samsung,A10 SWA OPEN 00", "samsung,exynos7885";
+	compatible = "samsung,sm-a105f", "samsung,exynos7885";
